Add lib/kernel/backing-issue.js: an idempotent, injectable primitive that
guarantees a branch/worktree has a backing Kernel issue without anyone
remembering to run `forge issue create`.

- Dedupes BY BRANCH: existing kernel_worktrees.issue_id linkage wins; a branch
  that encodes an existing issue id (e.g. feat/kap-7-foo -> kap-7) links that
  issue instead of minting a duplicate.
- Auto-creates a good-enough stub otherwise (title from branch, auto-stub label)
  and persists the branch->issue link into kernel_worktrees.
- Skips main/master, detached HEAD, and ignore-glob branches
  (tmp/spike/wip/throwaway) — returns null, creates nothing.
- Degrades to null (never throws) when the kernel is unavailable / non-kernel
  backend — safe to call from a hook.
- Fully injectable (driver/broker + clock/id source) for unit tests without a
  real repo. NOT yet wired into worktree/push/ship (that is PR2/PR3).

TDD: test/kernel/backing-issue.test.js (8/8 pass) covers idempotency,
skip-main, skip-detached, skip-ignore-glob, graceful degrade, the auto-stub
label, and a readable branch->issue link.

Design: docs/work/2026-07-06-auto-kernel-tracking/design.md
Kernel issue: 131ab014-8686-490c-a6b4-dc0989157d0c

